{
 "note": [
  "Word-motion cases measured on the real applications, one draft per row, through tmux",
  "in a workspace container (tmux send-keys -l <draft>, then M-b twice, C-a, M-f twice,",
  "C-e, M-BSpace once; the columns are what `tmux display-message -p '#{cursor_x}'` read",
  "after each key). `floor` is the cursor column of the empty composer, `back` the columns",
  "after each of the two backward word jumps from the draft's end, `fwd` after each of the",
  "two forward jumps from the floor, `kill` the column after one word delete from the end.",
  "Every number is the application's own answer, never the engine's. Rows marked `wide`",
  "hold 2-column glyphs, which the engine never predicts on; they are kept as measurements.",
  "Versions: zsh 5.9 (WORDCHARS empty), Claude Code 2.1.251, codex 0.150.1, Kimi Code CLI",
   "0.42.0, Muse Code 1.1.1, pi 0.84.3, fx 0.0.6, opencode 1.18.23. Re-measure with",
   "dev/scripts/README.md,",
  "'Word rules'."
 ],
